# Named providers and drivers

A provider or driver’s **own** page may name that product. Generic pages write the rule.

A passing instance is fine: “hosted providers (Supabase) reuse this driver.” Do not make a named product or a named driver pair the sample on a shared page.

## Do

- Use `id: "<product>"` or a made-up id on driver / API / “adding a provider” pages
- Link the product or driver page when the reader should open that one
- On a Pattern or recipe card, say “two drivers” / “a store”, not Postgres and Firestore

## Do not

- Put `id: "supabase"` (or Neon, etc.) in examples on the Postgres or API pages
- Build a generic section around one hosted product
- Write “Open Postgres and Firestore side by side” on a Pattern, recipe, or API overview

```ts
// Bad — Postgres driver page
postgres({ id: "supabase", connectionString });

// Good
postgres({ id: "<product>", connectionString });
```

```md
<!-- Bad — Pattern card -->
Open Postgres and Firestore side by side.

<!-- Good -->
Open two stores in the same workflow.
```
